ent-ImperialGlobeEarth = globe of Earth
    .desc = An old globe of Earth. Its faded surface seems to whisper that even towers, palaces, temples, and the world itself may one day vanish without a trace.
    .suffix = Decor, Hephaestus Station

ent-ImperialGlobeAres = globe of Ares
    .desc = A planet of the solar system, named after the Greek god of war.

ent-ImperialGlobeMoon = globe of the Moon
    .desc = Earth's natural satellite, once used as a proving ground for settling low-terrain-index worlds.

ent-ImperialGlobeEarth2 = globe of a blue-green planet
    .desc = A globe of a blue-green planet.

ent-ImperialBust1 = bust of an unknown employee
    .desc = I exist only because of the choices and sacrifices of others. There were so many of them, yet I do not know who they were. And how will my own choices shape those who come after me? Perhaps that is what it means to be human. Every species is part of history, but only we know it.

